 the previous holder, the British group Little Mix, by about 400 million streams, according to Guinness World Records.", "options": ["5.5 billion", "8.8 billion", "12 billion", "3.2 billion"], "question": "BLACKPINK set a Guinness World Record in 2023 by becoming the most-streamed female band on Spotify. How many streams did they have at that point?"}, {"source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cupid_(Fifty_Fifty_song)", "correct": 2, "fun_fact": "TikTok users had put the song in eight million videos by May 2023, and it later climbed to number 17 on the Billboard Hot 100.", "options": ["Twitter/X", "Instagram", "TikTok", "YouTube Shorts"], "question": "A sped-up version of FIFTY FIFTY's Cupid went viral on which platform in 2023?"}]$bank$::jsonb,
    verification_notes = 'Sources: https://www.nme.com/news/music/bts-dynamite-surpasses-one-billion-streams-on-spotify-2998803 ; https://www.nme.com/news/music/spotify-most-streamed-k-pop-songs-2024-bts-jimin-illit-stray-kids-3819059 ; https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/entertainment/k-pop/20200823/bts-dynamite-tops-global-top-50-on-spotify ; https://www.nme.com/news/music/blackpink-join-spotify-billions-club-how-you-like-that-3600941 ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gangnam_Style ; https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/entertainment/20250114/bts-becomes-first-k-pop-group-to-reach-2-billion-spotify-streams-with-dynamite ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hype_Boy ; https://www.nme.com/news/music/blackpink-most-streamed-girl-group-spotify-3410425 ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cupid_(Fifty_Fifty_song). Corrected on the owner''s request of 2026-10-27, every question checked at its source (docs/pending-migrations/quiz-team-fixes-2026-10-27.md).'
where id = 'e0965ec7-c7e6-4d67-bef5-a0f6ba46e25c' and published_quiz_id = 'bf101f43-30ff-4665-b85e-97a7fb0c105b';

update public.quizzes set questions = $quiz$[{"correct": 2, "fun_fact": "The video came out in April 2018, but the song itself was only released that August, on the album Love Yourself: Answer.", "options": ["Run", "I Need U", "Euphoria", "Spring Day"], "question": "In which BTS music video does Debussy's Clair de lune play before the song itself starts?"}, {"correct": 1, "fun_fact": "Its YouTube premiere drew more than 3 million viewers at once, a record for a music video premiere at the time.", "options": ["IDOL", "Dynamite", "Boy With Luv", "Permission to Dance"], "question": "Which MV features BTS in a colorful retro-disco setting?"}, {"correct": 3, "fun_fact": "By December 2020 the IDOL video had passed 800 million YouTube views, the fifth BTS video to get there.", "options": ["Pansori", "Buchaechum", "Samulnori", "Talchum"], "question": "Which traditional Korean mask dance appears in BTS's IDOL video?"}, {"correct": 1, "fun_fact": "A second video, for the song's remix, came out on June 1, 2018 and added extended footage to the original.", "options": ["Blood Sweat & Tears", "Fake Love", "Black Swan", "ON"], "question": "Which MV shows Jungkook searching for his bandmates in a maze-like manor full of decaying rooms?"}, {"correct": 2, "fun_fact": "The video also draws on Bong Joon-ho's 2013 film Snowpiercer, and it won Best Music Video at the 2017 Mnet Asian Music Awards.", "options": ["1984", "The Little Prince", "The Ones Who Walk Away from Omelas", "Norwegian Wood"], "question": "In the Spring Day MV, what book is referenced through the setting?"}]$quiz$::jsonb
where id = '7f0c64ca-a013-47a7-9620-52f7e741871b' and slug = 'bts-music-video-trivia-can-you-get-100';

update public.quizzes set questions = $quiz$[{"correct": 1, "fun_fact": "Nayeon released IM NAYEON in June 2022, debuting at #7 on the Billboard 200.", "options": ["Jihyo", "Nayeon", "Momo", "Chaeyoung"], "question": "Which TWICE member was the first to release a solo album?"}, {"correct": 1, "fun_fact": "POP! reached second place on South Korea's Circle Digital Chart and also made the top ten in several other Asian markets.", "options": ["ABCD", "POP!", "Dice", "Santa Tell Me"], "question": "What is Nayeon's debut solo single?"}, {"correct": 1, "fun_fact": "Fans call her Dance Machine, and in July 2023 she debuted in Japan with the TWICE subunit MiSaMo.", "options": ["Mina", "Momo", "Sana", "Jihyo"], "question": "Which member, considered TWICE's best dancer, was brought back into the lineup by Park Jin-young on Sixteen?"}, {"correct": 1, "fun_fact": "Mina studied classical ballet for eleven years, then spent a year at a K-pop dance studio before JYP scouted her.", "options": ["Momo", "Mina", "Sana", "Tzuyu"], "question": "Which member is known for her elegant ballet background?"}, {"correct": 1, "fun_fact": "Dahyun later trained at JYP Entertainment for more than three years before TWICE debuted in October 2015.", "options": ["Moonwalk", "Eagle dance", "TT gesture", "Heart shake"], "question": "A viral video of which dance first made Dahyun famous online?"}]$quiz$::jsonb
where id = '73249d20-b694-43c3-a3d8-72fd0aa9a4e5' and slug = 'twice-members-facts-quiz';

